All done. The fix is in `specs_setter::on_zero` (include/fmt/core.h:2351):

```cpp
FMT_CONSTEXPR void on_zero() {
  if (specs_.align == align::none) {
    specs_.align = align::numeric;
    specs_.fill[0] = Char('0');
  }
}
```

Previously the fill character was set to `'0'` unconditionally, even when an explicit alignment option (`<`, `>`, `^`) was present. Per the standard, when both are given the `0` flag must be ignored entirely — so both the `align::numeric` mode and the `'0'` fill are now only applied when no align option was specified.

